Ten bullets, seven rungs, and most of the page is not steps: bullets 5 and 6 are the healer menu options and a long description of the healer AI -- advice about how to drive the NPCs, not things the ladder can track. ZONE NAME NORMALISED, and this one matters: bullet 2 says only 'Travel to East Ronfaure', but bare 'East Ronfaure' resolves to the PRESENT-DAY zone (id 101), a different place from East Ronfaure (S) (id 81) -- I probed both through tools/pipeline/resolve.lua. Wings-of-the-Goddess campaign ops happen in the (S) zones, the header Description places the muster at East Ronfaure (G-5), and both nation siblings spell theirs out: Cut and Cauterize I (B) (page 41154) says 'Exit to North Gustaberg (S) ... at (K-8)' and Cut and Cauterize I (W) (page 42708) says 'Exit to West Sarutabaruta (S) ... to (I-9)'. So the step records East Ronfaure (S) at G-5. THE ENTRY ENTITY IS NOT NAMED HERE: bullet 3 says only that once the party leader selects to enter you are transported into Everbloom Hollow. Both siblings name theirs the Allied Ensign, but this page does not, and any string in target.name becomes a live marker key, so step 2 is {"type":"none"} with the sibling wording recorded in its note instead of guessed into the target. The two healers ARE named here -- the page writes '(Pupil Palliator I and II)', which expands to Pupil Palliator I and Pupil Palliator II -- and they are an unordered pair, so they share a group and both draw at once. The tier-I counts are 5 injured with the objective completing at 4. Bullet 9 (leave via the Dawn Aureola) is a real step, not advice: the page says you get no credit otherwise. Bullet 10 is the return-to-giver hand-in and the op is not over without it. Nothing here is observable -- no key item changes hands, healed-NPC counts are not in any packet. Header Time is 30 minutes. Campaign Rank here is 'Bronze Ribbon of Service' at one star (the star glyph is corrupt in the cached wikitext and renders as a section sign). Campaign rank is a real sign-up gate with no schema field, so it is noted and flagged and NOT written into gates.level, which stays null because the header's Level is 'Any'. This is the tier-I op: 5 injured, objective at 4 of 5, healed at 80% HP, and the page notes the healers have the MP for 4 but not 5 without resting. The only injured NPC this page names is the Royal Knight, called out as the furthest one and always enfeebled; one name out of five is not a ladder, so it stays in the note. Do not copy this ladder from a sibling tier -- II and III differ in every count. start.raw concatenates the Campaign Header's NPC Name / Zone / pos fields.

